1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,560
Conference Centre Reservations. Good morning.

2
00:00:02,560 --> 00:00:07,200
Hi. I'm interested in the computing conference next month.

3
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:09,210
Future Directions in Computing?

4
00:00:09,210 --> 00:00:13,740
Yes, that's right. Could I ask you a few questions about it?

5
00:00:13,740 --> 00:00:14,890
Of course.

6
00:00:14,890 --> 00:00:19,340
OK. I know the conference is for three days

7
00:00:19,340 --> 00:00:22,863
but actually I want to attend on the Friday and Saturday only.

8
00:00:22,863 --> 00:00:25,900
Will that work out to be any cheaper?

9
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:31,360
Let me have a look. Well, you could register for the two days separately,

10
00:00:31,360 --> 00:00:37,600
but that wouldn't actually save you very much as it still costs £35 for each day.

11
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:40,686
In fact, if you could register for the three days,

12
00:00:40,686 --> 00:00:44,640
you also get an invitation to a free dinner on the Saturday night

13
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:46,550
so that's probably the better option.

14
00:00:46,550 --> 00:00:51,570
Right, I'll do that. How much will the fees be in that case?

15
00:00:51,570 --> 00:00:53,600
It's £75.

16
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:57,880
All right. I'd like to register for the full three days

17
00:00:58,780 --> 00:01:00,910
Now, can I pay that by credit card?

18
00:01:00,910 --> 00:01:04,420
I'm afraid not. You'll have to send a cheque to us

19
00:01:04,660 --> 00:01:06,320
or you can pay at the conference office.

20
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:10,500
Fine. So it's probably easiest if I pay by cheque

21
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:14,974
Now then, what else do I need to arrange?

22
00:01:14,974 --> 00:01:20,440
Right. How about accommodation? I guess that's not included in the price?

23
00:01:20,440 --> 00:01:21,874
No, I'm sorry, it's not,

24
00:01:21,874 --> 00:01:26,750
but we do have a few rooms available for delegates at the conference centre if you'd like.

25
00:01:26,750 --> 00:01:30,563
Those are very cheap but if you're interested you'll need to book soon,

26
00:01:30,563 --> 00:01:32,910
because there's always a heavy demand for them.

27
00:01:32,910 --> 00:01:34,966
They are only £15 per night,

28
00:01:34,966 --> 00:01:39,700
but they are very basic and you'd have to get your own breakfast

29
00:01:40,120 --> 00:01:41,820
because they don't provide you with that.

30
00:01:41,820 --> 00:01:46,620
But it's very convenient, because it's in the same building as the conference rooms.

31
00:01:46,620 --> 00:01:47,440
Uhuh.

32
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:52,260
Or there's a very reasonable guest house which is £25 per night

33
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:54,180
And I think that includes your breakfast.

34
00:01:54,180 --> 00:01:56,680
Is it close to the conference centre?

35
00:01:56,680 --> 00:02:00,400
It would be about a ten-minute walk away from here.

36
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:03,890
I see. That sounds quite reasonable.

37
00:02:03,890 --> 00:02:07,800
The details are all in our conference pack, which I'll send you.

38
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:10,960
Great, thanks. That'll be very useful

39
00:02:11,580 --> 00:02:14,890
Oh, and can you also send me an application form?

40
00:02:14,890 --> 00:02:19,740
Of course. I'll get that in the post to you straight away. Is there anything else?

41
00:02:19,740 --> 00:02:25,690
Yes, actually. Can you tell me where exactly the conference centre is?

42
00:02:25,690 --> 00:02:28,260
Well, it's on South Park Road

43
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:30,830
and it's right at the end of the road next to the library.

44
00:02:30,830 --> 00:02:35,630
It's a ten-minute taxi ride from the station and will cost you £5.

45
00:02:35,630 --> 00:02:37,672
Otherwise, you can take the bus

46
00:02:37,672 --> 00:02:39,920
which runs every half an hour from the station

47
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:44,140
That's the 21A-and it brings you straight to the conference centre.

48
00:02:44,140 --> 00:02:45,900
Right, got that.
